package org.tc8.ets3

<** @description: Tester-side target service for §5.1.6 SOMEIP_ETS_097
  (SD_Client_restarts_tcp_connection). The DUT spawns a CommonAPI Proxy
  for this interface when `TC8_DUT_CLIENT_MODE=1` and triggers a
  `subscribe` on the TCP-reliable event when the tester invokes
  `clientServiceSubscribeEventgroup` (Method 0x32). vsomeip's SD client
  + endpoint manager handle FindService → SubscribeEventgroup →
  TCP-connect → retry-on-ECONNREFUSED autonomously, so the DUT firmware
  needs only the buildProxy + subscribe calls and no custom listener.

  SERVICE-ID 0xF4E9 (kept distinct from SERVICE-ID-1 0xF4E7 + SERVICE-ID-2
  0xF4E8 to avoid collision with the existing server-side instances).
  Single TCP-reliable broadcast under eventgroup 0x000A so the SubscribeEventgroup
  carries an IPv4 Endpoint Option with l4proto = 0x06 (TCP), which is what
  triggers the DUT's TCP-connect attempt that ETS_097 verifies. **>
interface ClientTarget {
    version { major 1 minor 0 }

    <** @description: TCP-reliable broadcast event. The Subscribe carries a
      TCP IPv4 Endpoint Option per PRS_SOMEIPSD_00362 because
      SomeIpReliable=true in ets3.fdepl. **>
    broadcast TargetEventReliable {
        out {
            UInt8 value
        }
    }

    <** @description: UDP-unreliable broadcast event used by §5.1.6
      SOMEIP_ETS_082 (server reboot with reassigned UDP port). The
      Subscribe carries a UDP IPv4 Endpoint Option because
      SomeIpReliable=false in ets3.fdepl. **>
    broadcast TargetEventUnreliable {
        out {
            UInt8 value
        }
    }
}
